drm/msm/dpu: single-slice DSC panels and plane check without virtual planes

Two 6.17 (sm8450-mainline next) display regressions on the Xiaomi 12,
whose panel (l3-42-02-0a) is driven with one 1080-wide DSC slice per line
(stock topology 1:1:1). The screen stayed black, then garbled.

1. Without virtual planes, the plane check computes the number of mixer
   stages from crtc_state's mixer count before the mixers are assigned,
   gets 0 and never fills pipe_cfg: every modeset failed with "invalid
   source 0x0+0+0" (-E2BIG), phoc's output test failed and the greeter
   aborted. Use one stage then, as upstream does since.

2. With DSC the CRTC always took two DSC encoders (and two mixers) per
   interface when the SoC has them. Two merged encoders split each line
   between them, which needs at least two slices per line; with a single
   slice the DSI got a different byte count per line than it expected,
   the command-mode transfer never finished (pp_done timeouts, DCS
   commands then failed with -110) and the panel showed the first lines
   followed by garbage. Mark single-slice configs in the encoder and use
   one DSC encoder for them.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index 2625ad777..dc219a8aa 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1366,7 +1366,14 @@ static struct msm_display_topology dpu_crtc_get_topology(
 		num_rt_intf--;
 
 	if (topology.num_dsc) {
-		if (dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= num_rt_intf * 2)
+		/*
+		 * Two DSC encoders per interface (merged) only work if the
+		 * panel's line has at least two slices; a single-slice panel
+		 * (Xiaomi 12: one 1080-wide slice, stock topology 1:1:1) got
+		 * garbage and every frame timed out.
+		 */
+		if (topology.num_dsc >= 2 &&
+		    dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= num_rt_intf * 2)
 			topology.num_dsc = num_rt_intf * 2;
 		else
 			topology.num_dsc = num_rt_intf;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 94b06c959..9c4d8a6c2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -676,11 +676,13 @@ void dpu_encoder_update_topology(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc,
 	dsc = dpu_encoder_get_dsc_config(drm_enc);
 
 	/*
-	 * Set DSC number as 1 to mark the enabled status, will be adjusted
-	 * in dpu_crtc_get_topology()
+	 * Set DSC number to mark the enabled status, will be adjusted in
+	 * dpu_crtc_get_topology(): 1 for a panel with a single slice per
+	 * line, which one DSC encoder has to compress whole, 2 when the
+	 * line can be split between two encoders.
 	 */
 	if (dsc)
-		topology->num_dsc = 1;
+		topology->num_dsc = dsc->slice_count >= 2 ? 2 : 1;
 
 	connector = drm_atomic_get_new_connector_for_encoder(state, drm_enc);
 	if (!connector)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
index 1cd3d04b1..de482323d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -893,7 +893,16 @@ static int dpu_plane_atomic_check_nosspp(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	 * rectangle left/right clipping first, then check wide rectangle
 	 * splitting in every half next.
 	 */
-	num_stages = (num_lm + 1) / 2;
+	/*
+	 * Without virtual planes the mixers are only assigned later in the
+	 * atomic check, num_lm is still 0 here and the loop below would never
+	 * fill pipe_cfg (every modeset failed with "invalid source 0x0+0+0").
+	 * One mixer pair is always needed then, as upstream does.
+	 */
+	if (dpu_use_virtual_planes)
+		num_stages = (num_lm + 1) / 2;
+	else
+		num_stages = 1;
 	/* iterate mixer configs for this plane, to separate left/right with the id */
 	for (stage_id = 0; stage_id < num_stages; stage_id++) {
 		struct drm_rect mixer_rect = {
